# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 7 (R3: a dynamic's update event fires at n with the value after n) and ch. 4 (a row reads its block's names): each click writes `$a`, and the row's `!Updated $c` fires in that tick.
test a_row_hears_its_blocks_parameter

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="bump")
    1/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x heard 0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x heard 1")

tick 2
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    1/["x"]/0: Ui.Label(text="x heard 2")
